      "id": "mem-MEMORY-media-messaging-architecture",
      "content": "- P2P sockets use length-prefixed framing: `[4B len][1B type][payload]`\n  - Type 0x01: JSON, 0x02: media chunk, 0x03: media request\n- Backward compatible: detects legacy raw JSON `{` first-byte\n- Media files stored in `~/Documents/p2pchat/media/{blake2bHash}.{ext}`\n- Swift writes compressed images to temp files, passes file paths to JS via IPC\n- Thumbnails (~15KB base64) embedded inline in message JSON for instant preview\n- Full images transferred via 64KB chunks over FramedSocket\n- Message.cont",
